;; 4.4.4). Every step is HKDF-Extract (an HMAC) or HKDF-Expand-Label over the committed objects through externs.
;;
;; hs_keys writes out[0..152): handshake_secret | c hs traffic | s hs traffic | c key 16 | c iv 12 | s key 16 | s iv 12.
;; ap_keys writes out[0..56): c key 16 | c iv 12 | s key 16 | s iv 12. finished_mac writes out[0..32).
;; Each returns 1, or 0 when an argument is refused or a step fails; on 0 the caller copies nothing (the C stopped at the
;; first failing step, the object runs them all, so only what lands in `out` on failure differs and the caller drops it).
;; A uint32_t length with a non-zero upper half is refused.
;;
